<title>GERMANY: Viag falls on telecoms loss speculation.</title>
<headline>Viag falls on telecoms loss speculation.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German diversified utility Viag AG fell over two percent in early bourse trade on Friday amid market speculation of higher-than-expected start-up losses in its telecommunications business.</p>
<p>Shares were down 16.50 marks at 758 marks in early bourse, while the overall DAX index was down 1.21 percent at 3,376.20 points.</p>
<p>&quot;There are rumours in the market that Viag's start-up costs are much higher than has been allowed for. This lowers its earnings potential,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>Viag has a telecommunications partnership with British Telecom.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
